### Page 2 of 2

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
May 9, 2024
demoed. The main entrance will be off Polk Avenue at the existing shared approach
and the Cheyenne Street access will be abandoned.
To grant a zone change, the Planning Commission must find one of three criteria
listed in Section 1-2-103(b) of the LCLUR. Two criteria has been met by the type of
development proposed and by meeting all of Planning's application criteria. Rezoning
is unlikely to adversely impact the area.
Brad Emmons, agent for the applicant, said the subject property had been a junkyard
but has been cleaned up. The owner now wants to establish a  storage facility for RV's
and boats and a zone change to LI is required. Mr. Emmons said the Cheyenne Street
access off the dirt road was planned to be left and used only as an emergency fire
access. If left, Public Works is requiring the applicant to pave Cheyenne Street. He
and his client feel if there is a secondary fire access off a dirt road it should not require
paving of that road. When they appear before the County Commissioners they plan to
ask that the Cheyenne Street access remain and not be required to be paved.
Mr. Emmons asked that when the changes to the Land Use Regulations come before
the commission for approval they consider including that if an applicant wants to use
an existing access off a dirt road as an emergency access they are not required to
pave the road.
Chairman Caughey opened the Public Hearing and receiving no comments the
hearing was closed and  a motion and discussion was called for.
A motion was made by Mark Smith, seconded by Natacha Gaspar to
adopt the finings of fact a and b of the staff report and recommend
approval of the Zone Change from AR to LI for the north 116 feet of Tracts
143 and 144, Sunnyside Addition, 5th filing, to the Laramie County Board
of Commissioners with no conditions.Vote 4-0.
Caughey, Stadel, Gaspar, Smith
Aye:
Watkins
Excused:
Adjournment
There being no further business the meeting was adjourned at 3:39 P.M.
CERTIFICATION
True and correct copy of the Minutes of the Proceedings for Thursday, May 9, 2024.
Approved by the Laramie County Planning Commission on Thursday, May 23, 2024.
